# Line-ending pins for files whose consumers care about the exact bytes.
#
# The sh sidecar script runs under bash on Linux/macOS CI runners; a CRLF
# working copy (which core.autocrlf=true would produce on a Windows clone)
# breaks bash with stray `\r`s if the file ever travels by any route other
# than a git checkout on the runner itself. Pinned LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is CR-tolerant both ways; workflows/YAML/Rust are fine under
# git's default text handling. Only the genuinely byte-sensitive case is
# pinned — a broad rewrite of the repo's eol handling is not this file's job.
